# What NOT to publish when the prototype is deployed.
#
# The deployed site is a public URL, so anything in the repo that is not part
# of the prototype itself would be browsable by whoever gets the link. These
# are dev tooling and reference material, not the thing being shared.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REAL PATIENT DATA — must never be published.
#
# Reference screenshots from the live gGastro system, containing patient
# names, a subscriber ID, dates of birth, a clinic address and a staff login.
# These are already excluded from git, so a GitHub-sourced deployment cannot
# reach them — but `vercel` run from this folder uploads the WORKING TREE, not
# the commit. Without this line that command would put PHI on a public URL.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Screenshot

# Local environment files. Gitignored, so a GitHub-sourced deployment never
# sees them — but this command uploads the working tree, which is the same
# reason the Screenshot rule above exists.
.env
.env.*

node_modules

# Dev tooling. Playwright never runs on the host, and the screenshot baselines
# are several MB of PNGs nobody reviewing the prototype needs.
tests
test-results
playwright.config.js

# Third-party design-system source, kept in the repo for reference while
# building the components. Not ours to republish.
Ref Components
refdummypage.html

# Database setup, not part of the prototype. It is run once by hand in the
# Supabase SQL editor and has no business being fetchable from the public URL —
# where its header would helpfully explain to a stranger exactly how open the
# row-level security on the comment table is.
supabase

# Local helpers.
Open Prototype.cmd
Open Prototype.command
.claude
